From 5685816894788dff476d522fda543fb799a81f02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 22:57:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00551/11171] [outer-loop] Stage exp3837 verifier-moat-at-scale
 into .354 (the decision-relevant research bet)

Adds the error-independence scissor AT SCALE alongside exp3833 in .354. exp3827
gave a preliminary "moat survives" (residual_catch=0.9000, overlap=0.5000) but on
a 100-item subset with suspiciously round numbers. Per the Adversarial-Confirmation
Discipline a score-300+ finding must replicate at scale with a CI before it is
paper-citable. exp3837: N>=1000, bootstrap CI95, two positive controls (reasoner
self-verify non-degenerate + carnot ensemble reproduces frozen 0.9131).

This is the single most decision-relevant research question for the DEFENSIBLE
deliverable (the verifier product): is Carnot's value error-INDEPENDENT of frontier
self-verification (durable moat) or does an o1-class model subsume it (DT-P2 risk)?

Live GPU (Qwen3.6-35B GGUF self-verification) -> requires_codex (gemini crashes GPU,
exp3703); verdict is a deterministic CI gate so codex suffices. .354 is now a 2-task
milestone: exp3833 (sound-lattice, CPU/$0) + exp3837 (moat-at-scale, GPU). Together
they characterize whether the verifier product is differentiated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
